# Trivy vulnerability-ignore list for the open-build-service-frontend image
# (used via --ignorefile in .github/workflows/open-build-service-frontend-rebuild.yml).
#
# WHY ALL OF THESE ARE ACCEPTED
# This image bakes the pinned open-build-service 2.10.34 release, which is built
# against the Rails 5.2.8.1 / Ruby 2.7 gem stack. openSUSE ships exactly these
# gem versions in its own OBS:Server:2.10 frontend container (the base image this
# one extends), so the versions are not something we can move independently --
# bumping any of them would mean forking OBS's src/api and re-resolving the whole
# Gemfile.lock, which breaks the "track the openSUSE 2.10 line" premise of this
# image. The CVEs below are therefore structurally unfixable in this image: the
# fix lives in a newer Rails/Ruby that OBS 2.10 does not ship.
#
# The set spans dev/test-only gems (selenium-webdriver, rdoc, uri) and core
# runtime gems (actionview, activestorage, activesupport, nokogiri, puma, ...).
# Accepted deliberately after review -- see the commit that added this file
# (in the original Gitea docker-images repo) for the Trivy report.
# Re-evaluate when (or if) OBS moves off Rails 5.2 / Ruby 2.7.
#
# Format: one vulnerability ID per line (CVE-... or GHSA-...). The gem test-
# fixture private keys (bunny, capybara, mysql2 spec .pem files) are NOT listed
# here -- those are Trivy *secret* findings, suppressed via --skip-files in the
# workflow (an ignorefile only affects vulnerability findings).

# actionview 5.2.8.1
CVE-2023-23913

# activestorage 5.2.8.1
CVE-2026-33195
CVE-2026-33202
CVE-2026-33174
